WEBVTT

00:00:00.598 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:04.990
Blow-drying is the last step of every hair service.

00:00:05.145 --> 00:00:08.669
And clients often judge the whole service by those last few minutes.

00:00:09.156 --> 00:00:13.230
A beautiful cut that is blow-dried frizzy still doesn't look good to the client.

00:00:13.658 --> 00:00:16.305
And blow-drying the wrong way damages the hair,

00:00:16.255 --> 00:00:18.350
and can even burn the client's scalp.

00:00:18.532 --> 00:00:22.928
Today, we will understand why the right blow-dry leaves the hair shiny,

00:00:22.878 --> 00:00:24.030
holding its shape,

00:00:24.122 --> 00:00:24.750
and safe.

00:00:25.357 --> 00:00:27.386
Why does blow-drying create a style?

00:00:27.847 --> 00:00:31.544
When hair is wet, water loosens small bonds inside the strand,

00:00:31.494 --> 00:00:34.426
so the hair bends easily into the shape you want.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:38.163
As the hair dries and cools, those bonds close again,

00:00:38.113 --> 00:00:40.266
holding the hair in its new shape.

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:42.986
There are a couple of things to remember from this.

00:00:43.336 --> 00:00:47.226
The hair must be completely dry, and cool, for the shape to hold.

00:00:47.405 --> 00:00:52.026
And when the hair gets wet again, or meets humid air, the shape gradually drops out.

00:00:52.645 --> 00:00:56.301
The surface of each hair has a cuticle layer, like roof tiles,

00:00:56.251 --> 00:01:00.024
overlapping each other, pointing from the root down to the ends.

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:04.643
When the air flows down from root to ends, the tiles lie flat,

00:01:04.593 --> 00:01:07.464
light reflects evenly, and the hair shines.

00:01:07.888 --> 00:01:11.623
When the air blows upward from the ends, the tiles are lifted,

00:01:11.573 --> 00:01:13.704
and the hair turns frizzy and dull.

00:01:13.889 --> 00:01:18.024
That is why the dryer nozzle always points down, along the hair shaft.

00:01:18.597 --> 00:01:21.383
A good blow-dry starts before you switch on the dryer.

00:01:21.772 --> 00:01:25.063
Blot with a towel, pressing gently, never rubbing.

00:01:25.503 --> 00:01:27.063
Detangle from the ends up.

00:01:27.506 --> 00:01:29.463
Then use a heat protection product.

00:01:29.732 --> 00:01:32.829
Spray or apply it evenly over the mid-lengths and ends,

00:01:32.779 --> 00:01:35.543
with the amount and method the product instructs.

00:01:35.972 --> 00:01:39.783
The product helps reduce damage, but it doesn't replace drying the right way.

00:01:40.084 --> 00:01:43.996
With heat that is too high, or drying one spot for too long,

00:01:43.946 --> 00:01:45.863
no product can save the hair.

00:01:46.477 --> 00:01:48.674
Don't pick up a round brush right at the start.

00:01:49.072 --> 00:01:50.890
Rough-dry with your hands first,

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:53.874
until the hair is about seventy to eighty percent dry.

00:01:54.287 --> 00:01:56.674
Only then section it, and use the brush.

00:01:57.072 --> 00:01:59.954
This is much faster, and the hair takes less heat.

00:02:00.463 --> 00:02:04.754
Using a brush on soaking wet hair takes longer, and pulls the hair a lot.

00:02:05.096 --> 00:02:06.594
Section as you do for a cut.

00:02:06.849 --> 00:02:09.154
Start at the nape, and work gradually up.

00:02:09.317 --> 00:02:12.429
Each section is no wider than the brush, and not too thick,

00:02:12.379 --> 00:02:14.194
so the air gets through all of it.

00:02:14.765 --> 00:02:15.798
The main brushes.

00:02:16.196 --> 00:02:17.478
A flat paddle brush:

00:02:17.586 --> 00:02:21.318
for straight, smooth drying, fast, with little volume.

00:02:21.732 --> 00:02:22.757
A round brush:

00:02:23.024 --> 00:02:26.118
for volume, a curve at the ends, or curls.

00:02:26.547 --> 00:02:29.638
A large round brush gives the ends a gentle curve.

00:02:29.986 --> 00:02:32.438
A small round brush gives curlier pieces.

00:02:32.699 --> 00:02:35.398
Many round brushes have a metal or ceramic core.

00:02:35.625 --> 00:02:39.268
The core heats up as you dry, helping to set the shape faster,

00:02:39.218 --> 00:02:41.238
but it also gets hot in your hand,

00:02:41.335 --> 00:02:42.278
and on the hair.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.758
Don't hold the brush against the client's scalp.

00:02:45.387 --> 00:02:49.254
The concentrator nozzle, the flat attachment on the end of the dryer,

00:02:49.204 --> 00:02:51.246
always goes on when you are styling.

00:02:51.735 --> 00:02:55.566
It focuses the air into a narrow band, right where the brush is working.

00:02:56.056 --> 00:02:59.782
The nozzle sits parallel to the brush, pointing down along the hair,

00:02:59.732 --> 00:03:01.566
a few centimeters from the brush.

00:03:02.135 --> 00:03:05.006
The dryer follows the brush, from root to ends.

00:03:05.197 --> 00:03:05.806
And tension.

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:10.366
The brush has to hold the hair with enough tension for it to come out smooth and shiny.

00:03:10.684 --> 00:03:12.846
But pull the hair, not the client's head.

00:03:13.169 --> 00:03:16.526
If you see the head leaning with the brush, you are pulling too hard.

00:03:17.142 --> 00:03:19.417
Many stylists skip the cool shot button.

00:03:19.817 --> 00:03:23.475
After drying a section with hot air, keep the section on the brush,

00:03:23.425 --> 00:03:25.737
and press the cool shot for a few seconds,

00:03:25.847 --> 00:03:26.857
so the hair cools.

00:03:27.114 --> 00:03:28.537
Only then pull the brush out.

00:03:28.938 --> 00:03:31.257
Hair that cools in that shape holds it longer.

00:03:31.634 --> 00:03:36.211
Pull the brush out while the hair is still warm, and the section easily relaxes,

00:03:36.161 --> 00:03:36.777
and drops.

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:38.867
Volume, or sleek?

00:03:39.332 --> 00:03:43.931
For root volume, lift the section up high, against the way the hair lies,

00:03:43.881 --> 00:03:45.426
and dry the roots first,

00:03:45.533 --> 00:03:46.867
so they dry standing up.

00:03:47.521 --> 00:03:52.851
For a smooth look, close to the head, pull the section down, close to the head,

00:03:52.801 --> 00:03:53.987
and dry downward.

00:03:54.165 --> 00:03:57.093
And for turning the ends under, as with a bob,

00:03:57.043 --> 00:03:59.907
the round brush works underneath the section,

00:04:00.183 --> 00:04:04.467
and at the ends, you turn the brush inward, so the ends curve under.

00:04:05.107 --> 00:04:07.283
Naturally curly hair is different.

00:04:07.657 --> 00:04:10.796
If the client wants to keep her curls, don't use a brush,

00:04:10.746 --> 00:04:12.963
and don't comb while the hair is drying,

00:04:13.149 --> 00:04:14.883
or the curls break up into frizz.

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:21.093
Use a diffuser, the large, round attachment with lots of prongs, on low airflow,

00:04:21.043 --> 00:04:22.243
and medium heat.

00:04:22.829 --> 00:04:26.789
Lift the hair up into the bowl of the diffuser, hold it still for a while,

00:04:26.739 --> 00:04:28.163
then move to another spot.

00:04:28.428 --> 00:04:32.483
Touch the hair as little as possible, until it is completely dry.

00:04:33.151 --> 00:04:33.932
About heat.

00:04:34.324 --> 00:04:37.612
Fine, fragile, colored or bleached hair:

00:04:37.861 --> 00:04:38.972
use moderate heat.

00:04:39.311 --> 00:04:43.452
Thick, coarse hair can take more heat, but you still have to keep the dryer moving.

00:04:43.867 --> 00:04:48.092
Never press the nozzle against the scalp, or hold it on one spot for too long.

00:04:48.442 --> 00:04:51.852
The scalp, the ears and the nape burn very easily.

00:04:52.281 --> 00:04:53.692
Ask the client now and then:

00:04:54.041 --> 00:04:54.892
is it too hot?

00:04:55.241 --> 00:04:57.692
And use the dryer as the manufacturer instructs.

00:04:58.267 --> 00:04:59.788
And think about your own body.

00:05:00.178 --> 00:05:04.828
A day of blow-drying many clients puts a lot of strain on your shoulders and wrists.

00:05:05.334 --> 00:05:09.228
Raise the chair to the right height, so your elbows stay below your shoulders.

00:05:09.577 --> 00:05:13.468
Stand with your back straight, feet slightly apart, wrists straight.

00:05:13.816 --> 00:05:16.668
Switch hands when you can, and choose a lightweight dryer.

00:05:17.326 --> 00:05:18.837
Finally, hygiene.

00:05:19.304 --> 00:05:23.363
After every client, remove all the hair from the brushes, wash them,

00:05:23.313 --> 00:05:25.957
and disinfect them as the product instructs,

00:05:26.226 --> 00:05:27.877
as in the lesson on cleaning tools.

00:05:28.219 --> 00:05:31.077
And clean the air filter at the back of the dryer regularly.

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:36.167
When the filter clogs with dust and hair, the dryer overheats, loses airflow,

00:05:36.117 --> 00:05:37.557
and breaks down sooner.

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:43.049
This lesson shares common experience from the trade, for training, and each country,

00:05:42.999 --> 00:05:44.037
and each school,

00:05:44.067 --> 00:05:45.317
works in its own way.

00:05:45.719 --> 00:05:48.597
And now, please take the short quiz below the video.

00:05:48.856 --> 00:05:49.716
See you next time.
